  "code": "2806",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\">Lyme disease is caused by a tick borne spirochete, Borrelia Burgdorferi.IgM antibodies may be detectable within 1-2 wks following the tick bite,but may be delayed for 3-6 wks,The IgM antibodies may be present for months. A negative result doesnot rule out the possibility of infection in a patient.Patient with clinical history / symptoms suggestive of Lyme disease may be retested in 2-4 wks.A positive result must be interpreted with caution.Cross reactivity has been seen with syphilis,relapsing fever Rocky mountain spotted fever,auto immune diseases,RA , SLE, CMV , EBV infection.The continued presence or absence of antibodies cannot be used to determine sucess or failure of therapy.</span></p>",
